From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Apr 2026 17:06:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cxa_exception.cpp: guard ASAN interfaces with __has_include
 for bare-metal

GCC 15 added __has_feature() support, causing __has_feature(address_sanitizer) to return true when NuttX KASAN (-fsanitize=kernel-address) is enabled. This triggers includes of sanitizer/asan_interface.h.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 src/cxa_exception.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cxa_exception.cpp b/src/cxa_exception.cpp
index 92901a8..cfc443e 100644
--- a/src/cxa_exception.cpp
+++ b/src/cxa_exception.cpp
@@ -284,7 +284,7 @@ __cxa_throw(void *thrown_object, std::type_info *tinfo, void (_LIBCXXABI_DTOR_FU
   __cxa_exception* exception_header = __cxa_init_primary_exception(thrown_object, tinfo, dest);
   exception_header->referenceCount = 1; // This is a newly allocated exception, no need for thread safety.
 
-#if __has_feature(address_sanitizer)
+#if __has_feature(address_sanitizer) && __has_include(<sanitizer/asan_interface.h>)
   // Inform the ASan runtime that now might be a good time to clean stuff up.
   __asan_handle_no_return();
 #endif
